  "pli-tv-bu-vb-pj2:7.25.2": "The unusual expression <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vutto vajjemi</i> recurs in the next two cases. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Vajjemi</i> is apparently an optative formation from <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vadāmi</i>, “I could say”, whereas <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vutto</i> is the past participle of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vuccati</i>, “spoken to”, the overall meaning being, “I, (having been) spoken to, could say to the family that supports you.” The idea conveyed seems to be the taking of a message. Sp 1.150: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Tava vacanena vadāmīti attho</i>, “The meaning is, ‘I will speak your statement.’” ",
